  * That is where a read can park the thread, which is exactly why it is a
  * separate level and why this runs in its own thread.
+ *
+ * Level 5 is the odd one: it never maps a register block at all. It asks the
+ * secure monitor which subsystems it will boot and returns, so the answer to
+ * "can this phone's TrustZone start the modem" arrives without the risk that
+ * came with every other level.
  */
 void
 polaris_modem_state_probe(void)
